@@ -6,6 +6,26 @@ adheres to [Semantic Versioning](https://semver.org/spec/v2.0.0.html).
 
 ## [Unreleased]
 
+### Smooth diode made passive; SPICE PWL diodes import as `add_diode(V_f=)`
+
+* **Fixed (BREAKING, numbers)** `add_nonlinear_diode` (`IdealDiode`)
+  sourced power: its law `logistic·(v − V_F0)/R_d` was negative for every
+  `0 < v < V_F0` (−1.392 A at 0.636 V at the defaults), so Newton saw a
+  negative conductance. A 20 V / 1 kHz half-wave clamp (10 Ω) aborted on
+  `engine='pwl'` at `dt = 1 µs` and read RMS 9.634 V on `trbdf2`. The law
+  is now `[sp(κ(v − V_F0)) − sp(−κ·V_F0)]/(κ·R_d) + G_off·v` (softplus):
+  `i(0) = 0`, `di/dv > 0`, same forward asymptote, same parameters. At the
+  defaults the current at 0.636 V goes from −1.392 A to +1.227 A, at
+  `V_F0` from 0 A to 3.466 A, at 1.0 V from 29.93 A to 30.01 A; the clamp
+  reads 10.010 V on both engines. The reverse current has a floor of
+  `sp(−κ·V_F0)/(κ·R_d)` (4.2 µA at the defaults).
+* **Changed (BREAKING, import)** `spice_to_builder` maps an LTspice
+  `Ron/Roff/Vfwd` diode to `add_diode(g_on=area/Ron, g_off=area/Roff,
+  V_th=0, V_f=Vfwd)` instead of the smooth diode: kind `StoredKind.Diode`
+  (was `NonlinearDiode`), a sharp knee at `Vfwd`, no Newton iteration,
+  visible to `res.i` and `device_loss_summary`. The `Vrev`/`Rrev`
+  refusals are unchanged.
+
 ### PWL diode forward drop (PSIM `V_f`)
 
 * **Added** `add_diode(..., V_f=0.0)` and the YAML `diode` key `V_f`: the
